<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <.legal_page id="terms-of-service" title="Terms of Service" updated="October 14, 2026">
    <p>
      These terms apply when you use the Octomocto website and its games. When you use
      Octomocto, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the website.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Octomocto is a free website with games that you can play alone or with other people.
      We can add, change or remove games and features at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can play without an account. If you sign in, you must give correct information and
      keep access to your email or Telegram account safe. You are responsible for all
      activity on your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Rules of conduct</h2>
    <p>When you use Octomocto, you must not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use a display name that is offensive, or that pretends to be another person.</li>
      <li>Harass or insult other players.</li>
      <li>Use bots, scripts or other tools to cheat or to play for you.</li>
      <li>Try to get access to data or systems that are not yours.</li>
      <li>Do things that can damage, overload or interrupt the website.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you do not obey these rules, we can remove your results, change your display name,
      or close your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The website, its design, the octopus characters and the Octomocto name belong to
      Octomocto. You can use the website for your personal use. You must not copy or
      distribute its content without our permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our <.link navigate={~p"/privacy"}>Privacy Policy</.link>
      tells you how we collect and use your data.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We supply Octomocto "as is" and "as available". We do not promise that the website will
      always be available, that it will have no errors, or that it will keep your results.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent that the law permits, Octomocto is not liable for any indirect,
      incidental or consequential damage, or for any loss of data, that comes from your use of
      the website.
    </p>

    <h2>End of use</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Octomocto at any time. To delete your account, send an email to <a href="mailto:hi@octomocto.com">hi@octomocto.com</a>. We can stop or close the
      website, or your access to it, at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If we change these terms, we will update the date at the top of this page. When you
      continue to use Octomocto after a change, you agree to the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about these terms, send an email to <a href="mailto:hi@octomocto.com">hi@octomocto.com</a>.
    </p>
  </.legal_page>
</Layouts.app>
